  "decision": "Determine which calibrated JEPA-derived Energy supports receding-horizon planning. The anchor is a one-step transition Energy trained on predicted successors with GAR ranking and 0.25 absolute advantage MSE. Each cell changes one factor: direct versus predicted state input, absolute-MSE weight, transition advantage versus transition distance versus state distance, or the geometry-only continuation-teacher horizon. Every checkpoint is evaluated on identical feasible-action interfaces with true global beam search at depths 1, 4, 8, and 16. Advance only cells that improve strict success consistently or explain the prior negative depth curve; then repeat decision-grade cells over five seeds.",
